WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.697
For eleven hours,

00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:03.899
Cursor's own extension store served

00:00:03.699 --> 00:00:05.367
a fake Claude Code that

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.761
planted backdoor keys.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:09.258
Uninstalling the extension leaves those

00:00:09.058 --> 00:00:09.967
keys in place.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:12.115
Cursor says up to five

00:00:11.915 --> 00:00:13.916
thousand users were exposed on

00:00:13.716 --> 00:00:15.926
October twenty-ninth, and it has

00:00:15.726 --> 00:00:17.035
pulled the package.

00:00:17.075 --> 00:00:19.056
Anthropic did not make the build.

00:00:19.606 --> 00:00:21.102
It looked like a routine

00:00:20.902 --> 00:00:22.646
update under Anthropic's name.

00:00:22.686 --> 00:00:24.529
Hidden code ran as Cursor

00:00:24.329 --> 00:00:26.173
loaded it, sent home a

00:00:25.973 --> 00:00:27.894
profile of the machine,

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.772
planted an attacker's SSH key

00:00:29.572 --> 00:00:31.337
and added startup hooks.

00:00:31.887 --> 00:00:33.646
Turning on the SSH server

00:00:33.446 --> 00:00:35.057
needs admin rights,

00:00:34.857 --> 00:00:36.765
and that step mostly failed.

00:00:36.805 --> 00:00:38.124
The key and the hooks

00:00:37.924 --> 00:00:39.572
needed none, so they ran

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.494
on most machines.

00:00:41.044 --> 00:00:42.644
If Remote Login is on,

00:00:42.444 --> 00:00:43.904
or someone turns it on

00:00:43.704 --> 00:00:45.724
later, the planted key works.

00:00:45.764 --> 00:00:47.799
Developers switch SSH on all

00:00:47.599 --> 00:00:48.334
the time.

00:00:48.884 --> 00:00:50.445
Search your SSH key list

00:00:50.245 --> 00:00:51.670
for the label shown on

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:53.235
screen, then look for the

00:00:53.035 --> 00:00:54.051
startup hooks.

00:00:54.091 --> 00:00:55.463
If you find either,

00:00:55.263 --> 00:00:57.676
disconnect and rotate credentials from

00:00:57.476 --> 00:00:58.783
a trusted computer.

00:00:59.333 --> 00:01:01.332
Coding tools now hold deep

00:01:01.132 --> 00:01:02.641
access on a laptop.

00:01:02.681 --> 00:01:04.496
Pin the extensions you rely

00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:05.971
on, and turn off silent

00:01:05.771 --> 00:01:07.937
auto-updates for deep-access ones.

00:01:08.487 --> 00:01:10.704
The complete five-minute check for

00:01:10.504 --> 00:01:12.303
Mac, Windows and Linux is

00:01:12.103 --> 00:01:13.416
in the full story on

00:01:13.216 --> 00:01:14.181
The Dispatch.

00:01:14.221 --> 00:01:15.582
Check your keys today.

